    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d252">

                <pb facs="0294" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.857 Athenia/116: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cudahy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-07">September 7, 1939</date>.<lb/>[Received September
                        7—8:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Your No. 15.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d252-f1"/> Read my open telegram from
                    Galway 2:25 p.m. September 5th<anchor n="78" xml:id="d252-f2"/> in which I made
                    report after interviewing several officers, members of crew and number of
                    passengers of <hi rendition="#italic">Athenia</hi>. My despatch setting forth
                    more detailed statement should reaffirm beyond question that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Athenia</hi> was torpedoed, this conclusion confirmed by
                        <pb facs="0295" n="287" xml:id="pg287"/> Captain Alan Kirk, Naval Attaché
                    London, who made independent investigation. Believe any further statement by
                    affidavit will be purely cumulative. Legation has American addresses of all
                    Galway survivors.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cudahy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
